This last one here is about using perfusion index to determine fluid responsiveness.

44
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:09,360
The next thing we can use perfusion index for is to facilitate the assessment of pain.

45
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:12,960
So again we won't get into the details here but just a couple studies.

46
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:17,840
This first one looked at the use of perfusion index for critically ill patients that are

47
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,480
not intubated.

48
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:25,860
This next one looked at perfusion index as an indicator of pain for patients under general

49
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:32,600
anesthesia but just to show that the data is not 100% consistent this last paper did

50
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:39,040
not find any correlation between perfusion index and pain as assessed by an alternative

51
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:41,380
assessment tool.

